{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities","id":1447740,"title":"Lowkey awesome Vampire cities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-06T17:56:43-07:00","id":1447740,"title":"Lowkey awesome Vampire cities","content":"Which, by Vampire canon underdeveloped and/or underappreciated, cities do you feel it would be awesome to set a chronicle in? A non-negotiable criterion must be that it has never had a &quot;By Night&quot; book. Preferably, it shouldn't have played a big part in the metaplot at all (so, Vienna and Venice would be out for example). Bonus points if it has an awesome opera house, because one of my players wants to play a phantom of the opera nosferatu.<br /> <br /> For me, Russia in general immediately comes to mind, due to it's fascinating history and extreme contrast between wealth and decay, beauty and ugliness. Russia is already like the West run through a World of Darkness filter. You almost wouldn't have to exaggerate.<br /> <br /> Las Vegas is an obvious choice as well, for a plethora of reasons, but I've already run a chronicle set there.<br /> <br /> Asia, of course, has a myriad of options, but please refrain from them in this thread, I feel strongly that V5 as currently written can only adequately portray Vampires in a more or less western context, plus I love Kindred of the East but currently don't know what to do with it.<br /> <br /> Please make a case for your suggestions by explaining what makes them awesome, and how vampires would fit into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T05:30:44-07:00","id":1447795,"title":"","content":"Vienna got a By Night Book during the German own Productions.<br /> I would say either Linz as it is the backturf of Karl Schrekt and the new Capital of the House Tremere or Salzburg the second most important city of Austria and another one with international importance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T05:44:26-07:00","id":1447799,"title":"","content":"Honestly I feel the architecture/urban planning of former soviet cities makes for poor vampires. Too decentralized, too open, too many old folks on the balconies. And it's not the 90's anymore, I couldn't find a stray dog to save my life. Maybe that's just my region. There are some pros: corruption is huge and every block looks like a fortress. It'd be too hard to hunt and paradoxically too easy to be targeted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2021, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T10:03:34-07:00","id":1447827,"title":"","content":"I feel like it is important to know the city. Not saying it is required, but it gives a better feel for how things...feel I guess. If you have driven the streets you know what traffic is like, how the buildings look, the types of stores and restaurants, how the food is made, how the people feel about things, etc... Even just a nice vacation would be helpful I think. TV shows set in an area can be helpful if they are actually filmed there and are not just a hollywood stereo type. It's why it was so advantageous to be from Chicago's south side, having been to Gen Con all those years in Milwaukee, Etc... the game really felt like it was meant for us.<br /> <br /> Anywhere the government turns a blind eye to violence, something like Portland would be ideal, and there are plenty of choices. I lived by Seattle and local news did a much better job of showing how great Seattle could be for vampires, especially Anarch and Sabbat games, than you might think given how upscale and expensive Seattle can be, if I never lived there I probably wouldn't even think of it.<br /> <br /> I really recommend thinking about somewhere you are familiar with over just random city that has a big population.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> <br /> That's interesting, are you from Russia? if not how long have you been living there? if you don't mind my being nosy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T11:03:38-07:00","id":1447831,"title":"","content":"I've been living in Lithuania for the past year (and a bit before that, I seem to move around a lot) . Baltic state, anexed by the soviets from WWII. I don't live in the capital, though I've visited, and there are still &quot;old towns&quot; in the centre of the cities here. We don't have the high-rise blocks of russia, 12 story buildings are the limit and rather rare, with most going for 9 or 5 (5 stories was popular because you didn't need to build elevators for them) but we're also, statistically speaking, heavily populated by depressed, suicidal alcoholics, and the population is aging because anyone young wants to leave.<br /> <br /> And as for the rest of your post, I'm reminded of a game I ran set in Atlanta. For most of my life till shortly after that point I've lived in places that are almost completely racially homogenous or at least well integrated. It was difficult to get my head around a setting where there wasn't a default assumption for race, there wasn't a different naming convention for each race, and yet race was important enough that I need to include it in the description whenever a crime occured.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JGVBv7svKLo\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JGVBv7svKLo</a><br /> A decent vid on soviet city planning","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-08-2021, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T12:47:44-07:00","id":1447835,"title":"","content":"Las Vegas you already named.<br /> <br /> Houston and the south in generally is very underdeveloped.<br /> <br /> Brazil has a lot of options.<br /> <br /> India has a ton of major cities that would make great settings<br /> <br /> South Africa would be good as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T13:32:52-07:00","id":1447837,"title":"","content":"ROME: The decadence and glory of a lost empire with many vampirical influence. An important capital in Europe, an state by itself, with the Vatican and the hunters threatening every misstep. I can imagine the tunnels of the Cloaca M\u00e1xima plenty of elders, and the mafias of Suburra fighting for the turf. It would be the first catholic Camarilla city, also, distancing the religion with the beastility of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> DAMASCUS: The Gehenna war, a cultural crossroad in middle east, an awesome melting pot where the kurds, the sunnies and the christian have been living in peace for centuries, but now are facing a ten years civil war. With elders buried in the sands, the Ashirra, the Camarilla, the Baali and the Sabbat, Damascus in the definitive battlefield of ideologies and sects in the 5th edition.<br /> <br /> VENECIA: The power base of the Giovanni, a political player for centuries that orchestrated the fall of Constantinople, the origin of the trading and capitalism in the west. Venecia combines the romanticism of the courts and the meetings of the Camarilla with the gothic menace of the things under the water, the premascine. Cloak, daggers and conspiracies in the elysium.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T13:56:57-07:00","id":1447840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities#post1447740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Las Vegas is an obvious choice as well, for a plethora of reasons, but I've already run a chronicle set there..</div> </div> </div> </div>Las Vegas already was a setting in Nights of prophecy, the two introductory short-stories of Guide of the Sabbat and the Guide of the Camarilla and the book of Mage named Fallen Tower Las Vegas (a by night of mage). It is ruled by the Camarilla and the jew Giovanni, the Rothsteins.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities#post1447740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, Russia in general immediately comes to mind, due to it's fascinating history and extreme contrast between wealth and decay, beauty and ugliness. Russia is already like the West run through a World of Darkness filter. You almost wouldn't have to exaggerate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But I agree with you in Russia, it would be a very interesting setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 05-07-2021, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T14:12:34-07:00","id":1447843,"title":"","content":"My vote would be Prague. It has an interesting history, fantastic architecture, and a world class opera house (the Estates Theatre). There's a lot you can do to develop it as a setting for Vampire. Another city with an Old World feel and tremendous history would be Budapest with its Hungarian State Opera House. I believe both have been mentioned occasionally in various supplements (like Transylvania By Night), but are essentially undeveloped.<br /> <br /> If you want something completely different, there is Sydney, Australia with its iconic opera house.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for something in the US, you can use Dallas/Fort Worth. It's a huge metro area in the US that has been neglected in game. Bass Hall in Fort Worth is a newer opera house, but it looks wonderful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T14:40:10-07:00","id":1447847,"title":"","content":"I would like to see some smaller cities, like Burton upon Trent where my sisters live. You know, someplace with Steven King aura. Inspired by St. Claire from Project Twilight","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-08-2021, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T17:48:33-07:00","id":1447873,"title":"","content":"Miami and the surrounding area, mostly just because I'm a fan of Carl Hiaasen's fairly bizarre crime novels. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T01:30:16-07:00","id":1447904,"title":"","content":"I'm going to second Portland, OR as an excellent city that has been oddly untouched in 30 years of Vampire (or even White Wolf as a whole). It's an interesting city in many respects---a unique city council form of government (with a long history of corruption---at one point there was an IRL scheme by Labor Unions to literally seize control of Oregon's government), zoning laws keeping it dense and compact despite its population and the largest amount of parkland in any city of its size (Forest Park, which is over 8 miles long, is hard by the city). And of course the iconic Mount Hood looms over the skyline like an American Fuji. Memphis, TN is a similarly sized city with an interesting local culture with its famous music scene and iconic skyline including the famous pyramid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T15:58:09-07:00","id":1447996,"title":"","content":"Baltimore, because I was a big fan of Homicide: Life on the Street back in the 90s. Also The Corner and The Wire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T23:55:08-07:00","id":1448025,"title":"","content":"St. Louis. Lots of urban blight running up against shiny skyscrapers and parks. The highest murder rate of any large city in the US. A huge influx of almost 100,000 Bosnian refugees since the 1990s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T16:11:10-07:00","id":1448080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1447831#post1447831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been living in Lithuania for the past year (and a bit before that, I seem to move around a lot) . Baltic state, anexed by the soviets from WWII. I don't live in the capital, though I've visited, and there are still &quot;old towns&quot; in the centre of the cities here. We don't have the high-rise blocks of russia, 12 story buildings are the limit and rather rare, with most going for 9 or 5 (5 stories was popular because you didn't need to build elevators for them) but we're also, statistically speaking, heavily populated by depressed, suicidal alcoholics, and the population is aging because anyone young wants to leave.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually visited Lithuania twice (it used to be extremely cheap to fly there from my town in Sweden, and perhaps it still is), as well as Belarus, and one of my friends there has a legit degree related to Soviet city planning, and took me on a fascinating tour showing and talking about various areas of Minsk. So this is an appealing option indeed. It helps, for Vampire purposes, that the history of Greater Lithuania is extremely cool as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T16:13:16-07:00","id":1448081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Busboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1447904#post1447904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to second Portland, OR as an excellent city that has been oddly untouched in 30 years of Vampire (or even White Wolf as a whole). It's an interesting city in many respects---a unique city council form of government (with a long history of corruption---at one point there was an IRL scheme by Labor Unions to literally seize control of Oregon's government), zoning laws keeping it dense and compact despite its population and the largest amount of parkland in any city of its size (Forest Park, which is over 8 miles long, is hard by the city). And of course the iconic Mount Hood looms over the skyline like an American Fuji. Memphis, TN is a similarly sized city with an interesting local culture with its famous music scene and iconic skyline including the famous pyramid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually a player in another game master's Portland chronicle. We've only just begun, but he seems to have realized the city's potential indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T16:17:23-07:00","id":1448082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1447840#post1447840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Las Vegas already was a setting in Nights of prophecy, the two introductory short-stories of Guide of the Sabbat and the Guide of the Camarilla and the book of Mage named Fallen Tower Las Vegas (a by night of mage). It is ruled by the Camarilla and the jew Giovanni, the Rothsteins.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but it's not like it has been explored in great detail, we basically just know who a few major players are. Or, well, I didn't know about the mage book actually, perhaps I should look into it if my Las Vegas chronicle picks up again after coronavirus. It's a shame, though, how much cool stuff about Las Vegas I learnt about after my campaign had already taken off...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T04:31:25-07:00","id":1448113,"title":"","content":"In Fallen Tower Las Vegas you could find many interesting pieces of information. Basically, the turf is divided between the Syndicate and the Traditions, with multiple chantries fighting for dominance. Back in the 90s, White Wolf published also Necr\u00f3polis Atlanta, a &quot;by night&quot; for Wraith the Oblivion with included an appendix with vampires, some of them have reappeared in Beckett Jyhad Diary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T05:08:14-07:00","id":1448118,"title":"","content":"Gary, Indiana.<br /> <br /> *pause*<br /> <br /> Oh come on, you knew I was gonna say it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T06:38:45-07:00","id":1448120,"title":"","content":"The middle east became very interesting after the beckoning and I look forward for a by night from this area. Otherwise, South America became very dull after the introduction of the uninteresting drowned legacies.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T10:01:49-07:00","id":1448433,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Paso%E2%80%93Ju%C3%A1rez\" target=\"_blank\">El Paso-Juarez</a>, on the Texas-Mexico border. It's a huge population center, with roughly 2.5 million people, a rich history, and whiplash-inducing dichotomies (El Paso was awarded &quot;Safest City in America&quot; at the same time Juarez was exhuming mass graves, including one with 16 decapitated bodies. For context, downtown El Paso is a 20-minute walk over a bridge to downtown Juarez).<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T01:47:19-07:00","id":1448492,"title":"","content":"My personal campaign has the title 'Edinburgh by Night' in all my notes. It's a small city so it's good for keeping things low level and has plenty of options for all the different splats. Plus there are several opera companies and a bunch of theatres both grand and small.<br /> <br /> One nice thing about running games in European cities is that there's a sense of depth to the history, you can delve deep into the past for your sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T19:19:21-07:00","id":1448559,"title":"","content":"Chicago by Night; it details the city and Milwaukee; in my games, I prefer to use familiar, allusions. Gotham City, The City of Angels, Monument-City, Liberty-City etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T01:49:26-07:00","id":1448572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1448492#post1448492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal campaign has the title 'Edinburgh by Night' in all my notes. It's a small city so it's good for keeping things low level and has plenty of options for all the different splats. Plus there are several opera companies and a bunch of theatres both grand and small.<br /> <br /> One nice thing about running games in European cities is that there's a sense of depth to the history, you can delve deep into the past for your sources.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I storytelled some time ago a chronicle in Edinburg during the Victorian Ages, it was a very inspirational setting for this era: The gothic architecture of black stone, the plague and the districts locked in the underground, the tales of Robert Luis Stevenson and the legends of the Dunsirn inspired by Sawney Bean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T14:31:47-07:00","id":1448805,"title":"","content":"I've never actually run a game set here in Edinburgh myself though I know a lot of its strange history, as I like having some unfamiliarity to make stuff up more readily, so it's always interesting seeing what other people do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","user":"Craig Oxbrow","date":". 05-24-2021, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T06:37:00-07:00","id":1449337,"title":"","content":"I've only been able to find a few references to San Diego in my perusal of the VtM books, mostly in relation to the Anarch/Camarilla conflicts in Los Angeles and California. From what I can tell between the supplements and the unofficial White Wolf wiki, it doesn't appear to have been covered in much detail. What I can find says this: during the founding of the Anarch States. Tara Kearny was Baron, though doesn't seem to have been particularly respected by either those in the city or the Barons of other territories. She got ousted by her rivals, moved to Oceanside to lick her wounds, then defected to the Camarilla, wiped out her rivals when they were weak from infighting, and installed herself as Prince. After that, depending on which edition you're looking at, she either still rules in San Diego, was killed during the Final Nights, or was abducted by the Baron of Los Angeles and hasn't been seen since (though there are rumors that she's met her Final Death).<br /> <br /> Other than that, I've found little to nothing about my hometown. That's not surprising, since San Francisco and Los Angeles are more iconic, more populous, more culturally influential and financially powerful, and both hold greater weight in the public imagination. I'm certainly not complaining, or arguing that it should have been more fleshed out since it obviously wasn't necessary to the story being told. On the other hand, I would think that it would be a bit more on the radar of Kindred society. Consider:<ul><li>While the population of the city itself is a bit over 4 million, the city also has 35 million tourist visitors over the course of the year, making it a prime feeding ground. This number is further bolstered by the number of military personnel from surrounding bases who visit the city on leave, and a large population of undocumented immigrants who survive within the city's shadow economy.</li> <li>Much like El Paso upthread, San Diego is a significant border town. In campaigns where the Sabbat still claim rulership over the major Mexican cities, this territory is going to be on the front lines of any major war between them and their rivals in the Camarilla or among the Anarchs.</li> <li>As a major international center of trade, San Diego is going to be a target of interest for the Ventrue and any other Kindred interested in the acquisition of material wealth and financial power. It's also a playground for the wealthy, with a number of CEOs and multi-billionaires either living full- or part-time in high-priced communities such as La Jolla and Rancho Santa Fe.</li> <li>The Navy maintains a major base in San Diego, as well as many other facilities separate from the main base itself. The Marines have Camp Pendleton to the north in Oceanside, the Marine Corps Recruit Depot in the city itself, and the Miramar Marine (formerly Naval) Air Station. This is an obvious source of blood and useful ghouls, but also potential progeny for the Banu Haqim, Brujah, Gangrel, and other clans who traditionally place an emphasis on strength, martial prowess, and ability to survive.</li> <li>The nightlife and party scene is as expansive and varied as one would expect from a tourist city that also has three major universities (UCSD, USD, and SDSU), a constant influx of military personnel, and a large number of young, active professionals who reside in condos along the beach and in downtown lofts. At one point in the 1990s, Garnet Avenue in Pacific Beach allegedly had more bars per block than any place in the U.S. outside of New Orleans, though I can't verify that fact, and don't know if it's still true even if it was the case at the time. Either way, there's no shortage of areas to qualify as The Rack.</li> <li>The art scene in San Diego isn't large or well-known in comparison to other cities, but it's remained vibrant and consistent for many years, from Shakespeare at the Old Globe in Balboa Park to slam poetry readings at coffeehouses and Art Walks in various neighborhoods, a Toreador has plenty to work with.</li> <li>Comic Con, Comic Con, Comic Con. Toreador with interests in popular art, movies, and television. Ventrue looking after their financial interests in the entertainment industry. Tremere investigating how their occult insights somehow ended up in the pages of a web comic with an almost literal cult following. Nosferatu being able to wear full face coverings and mingle without anyone looking at them askance (2020 notwithstanding). Malkavians actually <i>blending in. </i>And, of course, the fans, an enormous number of whom are willing and possibly even experienced Blood Dolls. I can't imagine a number of Kindred NOT being in attendance, though a Prince would likely forbid any feeding at the Convention Center, the common areas of surrounding hotels, and anywhere related events were being held.</li> </ul>That just scratches the surface. There's also the enormous homeless population drawn to the idea of not actually freezing to death during the winter months, biker gangs in the outlying areas of the county, and a host of other items that are ripe source material for characters, adventures, and entire campaigns. Just a few:<ul><li>Most obviously, if Prince Tara is no longer in the picture, then who is in charge? What sort of struggle is happening among the local Primogen? Are the Anarchs going to seize the opportunity to reclaim their lost territory? Are the Sabbat, if they remain a factor, looking to take advantage of the turmoil?</li> <li>Since 1983, five mayors or acting mayors of San Diego have resigned, four of them as a result of scandal, and one after only three days of serving in an acting capacity. Was this simply bad luck (or bad judgment) on the part of the voters, or were other machinations going on behind the scenes to cause this repeated chaos?</li> <li>Exactly how have the Anarchs and Camarilla kept the Sabbat from sneaking over the porous border for the past several decades? Is there a truce of some sort, whether spoken or unspoken? Is the border neighborhood of San Ysidro essentially a no man's land, or possibly a demilitarized zone? Or does this have something to do with how human smugglers and traffickers really got the nickname of &quot;coyotes?&quot;</li> <li>What was with the fires set through Balboa Park in 1978, ones that resulted in the destruction of both the Globe Theatre and the Aerospace Museum? Human arsonist? Hunter who had narrowed down the possibilities of the location of a vampire's haven? Sabbat trying to invade or make a point with their typical panache? Or something even more sinister?</li> </ul>There's plenty more out there, from the decades it took to approve a new downtown library despite widespread support from the community (I think that someone's haven and feeding ground was in danger) to the stunning redevelopment of downtown from a blighted area to prime real estate (I can only imagine that this had something to do with the shift to the Camarilla). As far as the answers to these questions go, I have ideas, but that's best saved for another thread. I'll post them if I have enough interest in doing so, or others are interested in exploring the possibilities.<br /> <br /> If anything I've written isn't up to date or is inaccurate regarding the actual canon, I apologize. I've done my best to track down references to San Diego in the available material, but it's entirely possible that I missed something. If any WoD supplement (VtM or otherwise) that you know of has further information regarding the city, I'd love to know where to look. While I'm not slavish about following metaplot, I do like to get it as close as possible to the game setting, even if it's all going to fall apart upon first contact with the actual players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25574,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","user":"Heinrich Mentius","date":".  MARINE Air Station, not Naval Air Station. 05-23-2021, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T17:04:05-07:00","id":1450100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1447873#post1447873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Miami and the surrounding area, mostly just because I'm a fan of Carl Hiaasen's fairly bizarre crime novels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Miami was one of my two cities of choice, back in the day. (The other was Denver, 'the mile-deep city', run by a Nosferatu who dwelled over a seemingly bottomless pit in a played-out mine under the city.)<br /> <br /> For Miami, I tried to work in some local flavor, as well as making it a 'pact city' trapped between a Camarilla/Sabbat status, with factions of both present in a weird sort of cold war state (because the game at the time was going to have some players from each faction, temporarily united against a greater threat). In between some more serious stuff (like a mad Ventrue living in Coral Gables, who considered it his own personal fiefdom and everybody else just kind of ignored and let him call himself 'Prince' even though he very much wasn't), there was some over the top stuff like a Nosferatu who bred ghoul 'gators in the Turkey Point nuclear facilities cooling ponds.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T18:03:02-07:00","id":1450243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1450100#post1450100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Miami, I tried to work in some local flavor, as well as making it a 'pact city' trapped between a Camarilla/Sabbat status, with factions of both present in a weird sort of cold war state (because the game at the time was going to have some players from each faction, temporarily united against a greater threat). In between some more serious stuff (like a mad Ventrue living in Coral Gables, who considered it his own personal fiefdom and everybody else just kind of ignored and let him call himself 'Prince' even though he very much wasn't), there was some over the top stuff like a Nosferatu who bred ghoul 'gators in the Turkey Point nuclear facilities cooling ponds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned Miami's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1381358-ages-of-darkness?p=1434799#post1434799\">cocaine wars period</a> in my Ages of Darkness thread. It makes a pretty fascinating set up where you can potentially have the Camarilla, the Sabbat, the Anarchs, and the Setites (and possibly other factions, including Lupines) all constantly fighting, allying, and betraying each other depending on which way the wind blows that evening. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T09:46:16-07:00","id":1451226,"title":"","content":"Miami and Baltimore are both excellent suggestions people beat me to. Nothing like a quirky port city with a cool cultural identity and a history of violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T09:27:54-07:00","id":1451450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1451226#post1451226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Miami and Baltimore are both excellent suggestions people beat me to. Nothing like a quirky port city with a cool cultural identity and a history of violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Places like Cleveland, New Orleans, and Seattle work for similar reasons, as do cities like Amsterdam, Cape Town, or Kobe (which isn't so much violent as it is home to Japan's largest yakuza organization).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T18:37:16-07:00","id":1453423,"title":"","content":"to be honest i would want the world to be rid of <a href=\"https://quizlagoon.com/quiz/vampire-diaries-quiz/?utm_source=forums&amp;utm_medium=Anthony\" target=\"_blank\">vampires</a> as well i would have sided with esther. all vampires to is kill. they drain innocent life so they can survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26874-june20211","name":"june20211","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T19:45:55-07:00","id":1453425,"title":"","content":"Milwaukee aside, I'd like to see more published material about cities in the rust belt. They'd be fertile ground for examining how deindustrialization and rapidly-shifting demographics have wrenched Kindred society in modern nights, and how Sabbat-Camarilla-Anarch conflict impacts that. Detroit, despite having been mentioned in several books, has never had a &quot;By Night&quot; book and that's incredibly promising territory.<br /> <br /> I'd personally like to see more stuff regarding the South, in places that aren't Atlanta or New Orleans. Or Florida, for that matter. Two places I've always thought would be really cool to examine would be Knoxville, TN, and Huntsville, AL, for the same reason: their proximity to locales important to WWII and the Cold War (Oak Ridge and Redstone Arsenal, respectively). That could have some really cool implications for inter-sect conflict, conflict between vampires and hunters, or even changing up which clans <i>really</i> matter in those locations.<br /> <br /> I've mentioned before I'm fond of having Lasombra get obsessed with space in modern nights, the same way they get obsessed with the sea. In one chronicle a long time ago, I'd written up that a single Lasombra elder basically single-handedly took over the entire domain of Huntsville, AL, in the '50s and forbade any other vampire from entering the city on pain of Final Death, except for this lone Tremere chantry that was populated by physicist and computer scientist apprentices and their regent. Then one night the Lasombra just disappeared and was never seen again, and rumors persist the Lasombra sneaked onboard a rocket in tenebrous form and got launched to space.<br /> <br /> It was almost certain the Lasombra wasn't actually the first vampire astronaut and it got tagged by an enemy or rival, and even if it did go to space, it almost certainly met Final Death doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T20:04:52-07:00","id":1453428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1453425#post1453425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Milwaukee aside, I'd like to see more published material about cities in the rust belt. They'd be fertile ground for examining how deindustrialization and rapidly-shifting demographics have wrenched Kindred society in modern nights, and how Sabbat-Camarilla-Anarch conflict impacts that. Detroit, despite having been mentioned in several books, has never had a &quot;By Night&quot; book and that's incredibly promising territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how heavily first edition Vampire focused on the region, I have in the past pondered the idea of the rest of the WoD following suite and having Werewolf's signature setting be Rage Across Michigan, Mage focus on the Twin Cities, Wraith have Necropolis: Cleveland, and Changeling get Toronto. This was semi-jokingly followed up on by the idea that everything outside the Midwest is strange and exotic, with Kindred of the East describing the strange ethnicly orriented vampires of the Eastern seaboard (who are kind of a mash up of Lasombra and Giovanni, with a lot of Catholic religious overtones). Then the South is a Setite/Tzimesce Southern Gothic mix, and the West is Assamite/Ravnos nomad gangs.<br /> <br /> in hindsight , I sometimes wonder if Detroit would've made a better Sabbat signature city than Montreal. And Isay this as someone who thinks Montreal is a cool setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T07:37:09-07:00","id":1453452,"title":"","content":"Should've said this a while back; Manchester and Birmingham <br /> <br /> They've got a lot. Racialy diverse, Architecturally diverse, plenty of old buildings alongside new ones. You've got libraries that wouldn't look out of place in hogwarts and then you've got glass monstrosities. The streets are dirty. The wealth gap is high. You've got all the things you'd want in a WoD city except copious firearms, The accents are varied yet you still feel like you're in Britain (london, in a lot of ways stands rather apart from the rest of the country.) <br /> <br /> were I to write a city book for london, and I wouldn't, it would have multiple fully realized principalities and the centre would be like a sort of Vatican that few are permitted to enter. It's just too big. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T17:11:30-07:00","id":1453493,"title":"","content":"Marseille in France, which is one of the oldest inhabited cities in Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T00:55:17-07:00","id":1453526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1453493#post1453493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marseille in France, which is one of the oldest inhabited cities in Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, and considering how deeply divided it is between rich and poors, it's already WoD material <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T08:22:12-07:00","id":1453556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1453428#post1453428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in hindsight , I sometimes wonder if Detroit would've made a better Sabbat signature city than Montreal. And Isay this as someone who thinks Montreal is a cool setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easily one of the most interesting plot points in the &quot;V20-to-V5 development pipeline&quot; that seems to have been dropped to avoid political controversy, is the Ashirra making a play for Detroit, using the metro area's Muslim and immigrant population growth as basis for expanding its influence. From a storytelling perspective, that's a damn goldmine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T10:44:31-07:00","id":1552203,"title":"","content":"4 years later: What would you all want now?<br /> <br /> I would love the following in no real order.<br /> <br /> United States- Detroit, would love to see how it works Anarchs etc. Miami- My hometown, especially now that it is no longer Sabbat. Some place like Knoxville, TN or maybe Dallas, TX some place that no doubt has some flair to it.<br /> <br /> South America- Rio by Night, how do the Toreador do it, a party city open to all or by invitation only?<br /> <br /> Europe- Prague or maybe Edinburg both fantastic cities with great history.<br /> <br /> Australia- Brisbane would be cool to see 3rd or 4th in population how does little brother stand up to the big two rivals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T11:40:46-07:00","id":1552207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justicar-Seth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1552203#post1552203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">South America- Rio by Night, how do the Toreador do it, a party city open to all or by invitation only?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it, why a &quot;party city&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T11:55:02-07:00","id":1552210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1552207#post1552207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't get it, why a &quot;party city&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> Rio de Janeiro is widely recognized as one of the world's premier party cities, particularly renowned for its vibrant nightlife, cultural celebrations like the Rio Carnival, and lively samba scene, with the Lapa neighborhood serving as its nightlife nucleus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T20:34:39-07:00","id":1552225,"title":"","content":"I would like to see more Canadian Cities get some more love. In our game we play in the city of Calgary as it's large enough to support a decent sized kindred population and enough big business for a enterprising kindred to work with and it's old enough to have a handful of Anciliea being the top dogs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T05:53:14-07:00","id":1552227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1453428#post1453428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given how heavily first edition Vampire focused on the region, I have in the past pondered the idea of the rest of the WoD following suite and having Werewolf's signature setting be Rage Across Michigan, Mage focus on the Twin Cities, Wraith have Necropolis: Cleveland, and Changeling get Toronto. This was semi-jokingly followed up on by the idea that everything outside the Midwest is strange and exotic, with Kindred of the East describing the strange ethnicly orriented vampires of the Eastern seaboard (who are kind of a mash up of Lasombra and Giovanni, with a lot of Catholic religious overtones). Then the South is a Setite/Tzimesce Southern Gothic mix, and the West is Assamite/Ravnos nomad gangs.<br /> <br /> in hindsight , I sometimes wonder if Detroit would've made a better Sabbat signature city than Montreal. And Isay this as someone who thinks Montreal is a cool setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> While I think the \u2018Midwest Only\u2019 approach should never be official policy for the actual game line, this region-centric approach would be a delightful entry in the \u2018Black Dog games as parody of whomsoever is running the World of Darkness these days\u2019 genre.<br /> <br /> My own suspicion is that each \u2018Splat\u2019 ought to get their own section of the USA and the wider world, neighbouring and never entirely separate, but sufficiently far apart to allow each region to retain the distinct flavour of their game line.<br /> <br /> (One admits to believing that the various game lines - the Big Boys like VAMPIRE, WEREWOLF and MAGE, at least, work best as their own parallel timelines/alternate earths entire to themselves).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-09T10:22:23-07:00","id":1552234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447740-lowkey-awesome-vampire-cities?p=1552227#post1552227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own suspicion is that each \u2018Splat\u2019 ought to get their own section of the USA and the wider world, neighbouring and never entirely separate, but sufficiently far apart to allow each region to retain the distinct flavour of their game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. \ud83e\udd14 Vampire gets the Midwest, with Chicago as its signature city, Milwaukee as the Anarch haven, and Detroit as the Sabbat stronghold.<br /> <br /> Werewolf gets the Pacific Northwest, with Seattle as its signature area, and maybe later Vancouver and Alaska.<br /> <br /> Mage gets California, with LA as the signature city, and later Vegas and San Francisco.<br /> <br /> Wraith gets the Southeast, with New Orleans as its signature setting, and maybe later Atlanta and a regional book about Appalachia.<br /> <br /> Changeling gets New England, with Boston as the signature city, and maybe stuff about Vermont, Maine, Rhode Island, or the Maritime Provinces.<br /> <br /> Then NYC as a WoD book covering everybody.<br /> <br /> Not sure how the rest of the world would shake out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T03:23:33-07:00","id":1552258,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m tempted to suggest flipping Mage &amp; Changeling (C\u2019mon, Los Angeles and Las Vegas are almighty hubs of Glamour, the pixies are going to be drawn like moths to a bare bulb - and both cities are more than dangerous enough to fuel some interesting clashes between dreams, nightmare and banality), though I\u2019m not sure relatively-liberal New England has quite the right \u201cNo, this is Reality\u201d quality Mage needs to ground the Paradigm in everyday cynicism, banality and conformism,<br /> <br /> Still, your suggestions are rather good (It amuses me to imagine WEREWOLF getting All Canada, mostly because the dissonance between primordial Garou and relatively modest everyday Canada amuses me - while also allowing so interesting food for thought in terms of pointing out that the Great White North isn\u2019t as squeaky-clean as popular imagination makes it).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}